{"id": "EUVD-2026-103798", "enisaUuid": "1ad01fb2-6e34-3b9c-a69b-21703303b9d0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring: fix task_work add use-after-free with SQPOLL\n\nFor SQPOLL, the sqpoll thread runs task_work off its own list and\ndoesn't need to be told about it, so it can pop and complete a request\nas soon as mpscq_push() has published it. If that was the last request\nholding the ring alive, io_ring_exit_work() then frees the ctx, stops\nthe thread, and with it the tctx, while io_req_normal_work_add() is\nstill looking at both after the push:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in io_req_normal_work_add+0x439/0x510\n  Read of size 4 at addr ff11000000ca0000 by task repro/55\n  (...)\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in queue_work_on+0x25/0x70\n  Write of size 8 at addr ff11000000c3bd00 by task repro/55\n\nHold an RCU read lock across the add, like io_req_local_work_add() already\ndoes, and have io_ring_exit_work() wait for a grace period for SQPOLL rings\nas well before freeing the ctx.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:51:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:26:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42b3332efacfd2140be4cd0dedad4fb96b8ae90e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/891bd8335a0de3bb15c3b797ce3026bbb0dbef6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/395b25968fe854d4efaa19a8e9b7a5b6d1b3eea3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a92193c91e8839fe5fc209616ea95465ae4b919d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98858", "GHSA-v42g-qm29-227m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3143c0bb-7720-3d06-a854-d3afc529171a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "653c47f4-273d-33be-a9b6-9fe30e5b5e4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "6eb658b3-f591-33f2-913c-4b583ef49387", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "af5d68f8892f8ee8f137648b79ceb2abc153a19b <a92193c91e8839fe5fc209616ea95465ae4b919d"}, {"id": "9fce15f9-8339-30bd-9760-bf8a5aeb30d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "d199a491-23a0-3eef-a87c-75ab2f69bfad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "d6021fb3-ccd0-33aa-95dc-c52588c00693", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "af5d68f8892f8ee8f137648b79ceb2abc153a19b <891bd8335a0de3bb15c3b797ce3026bbb0dbef6c"}, {"id": "d87ae593-5d06-39ad-acb0-d438f4dc7b03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "af5d68f8892f8ee8f137648b79ceb2abc153a19b <395b25968fe854d4efaa19a8e9b7a5b6d1b3eea3"}, {"id": "dc59e4e5-d5ac-3ded-a18b-ccda9ee962e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "f7728e57-c3cb-3dcb-8f99-397f3d07a0d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "af5d68f8892f8ee8f137648b79ceb2abc153a19b <42b3332efacfd2140be4cd0dedad4fb96b8ae90e"}, {"id": "fbafc529-ce33-36cc-8b70-a5c4d6401334", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "097352e3-96f3-3822-bfa3-4fd91da8e607", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}